(1) Lemma 1.1 on 300 random scaffolds (horizon 3, STOP at any step, adaptive inputs, semimeasure samplers with 'no answer'):
    leaf probabilities sum to 1 exactly: True ; runs with no call occurred: True
    Lemma 3.2(a) (Scheffe) for run laws, with strict set and with ties added ( 219 trials had ties): max error = 0
(2) Lemma 2.1, exact binomials, N in {1..300}, q in a grid that contains 0 and 1:
    max Pr[Qhat >= x]/exp(-N kl) = 1.000000, max Pr[Qhat <= x]/exp(-N kl) = 1.000000 (must be <= 1)
    max Pr[kl(Qhat||q) > a]/(2 e^-Na) = 0.745912; max one-sided/(e^-Na) = 0.999999 (must be <= 1)
(3) Lemma 2.2 (i), (ii), (iii) on a 201 x 201 grid including p, q in {0, 1}: violations = 0
(4) Corollary 2.4(a),(b),(c) at the end points of {q : kl(phat||q) <= a} for 20000 random (phat, a): violations = 0
    Corollary 2.6(ii),(iii) for Q(R), Q'(R) anywhere in that interval: violations = 0; largest |Q'-Q|/bound = 1.0000
(5) Theorem 2.5 for one test, exact binomials (eps = pi*delta):
    (a) max failure/eps = 0.6261 (<= 1);  (b) max failure/eps = 1.0000 (<= 1)
    (c) joint: max failure/eps = 1.2500 at (N, eps, q) = (1, 0.8, 0.2231435736285649)  (the draft claims <= 1; the file proves <= 1.5)
    (c) joint, restricted to eps <= 0.2: max = 0.9987 at (1000, 0.2, 0.001609)
    counterexample N=1, delta=0.905, Q(R)=0.2: tol = 0.6297, ln(1/delta)/N = 0.0998; run in R: |1-0.2| = 0.8 > tol: True; run not in R: Q(R) = 0.2 > 0.0998: True; so the joint statement fails with probability 1
    sup of joint failure/eps over N <= 4, eps in (0,1), q on a grid: 1.3441 (the proved constant is 1.5)
(6) Remark 2.7(4): M independent events of probability 1/2, N runs; exact probability that the largest |Qhat - 1/2| is at least t:
